Ladybird now decides whether to include an SVG element in the
accessibility tree from its role token alone, without computing
its accessible name. None of the other engines computes a name for
that either. Blink’s AXNodeObject::ShouldIncludeBasedOnSemantics()
includes an element with role region whatever its name. WebKit’s
AccessibilityNodeObject::determineAriaRoleAttribute() treats an
unnamed region or form as having no role, but decides “unnamed” with
hasAccNameAttribute(), an attribute check. And Gecko’s ARIAMap.cpp maps
region to roles::REGION with no name check; only an HTML section’s role
depends on NameIsEmpty().
